  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation applied because scripts could not be run. Present design has multiple U-to-S3 paths: public issue or repository content can reach shell execution, branch push, and self-configuration under A4 autonomy with null step limits and an org-wide PAT. The only declared preventive control is behavioral prompt text, so residual falls one tier from critical to high under rubric step 4. Forecast is critical because the prompt control decays under model_upgrade and longer_task_horizon, and because planned Slack MCP addition would open another direct exfiltration sink. The single control whose decay most increases forecast exposure is ctrl.no_exfil_prompt."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and configuration in the provided prompt, config, and runtime notes, not observed runtime behavior.",
    "No source code, tool schemas, MCP manifests, audit configuration, or runtime telemetry were provided, so confidence is reduced where exact data flow and logging behavior must be inferred.",
    "Repository file trust was inferred from the public-repo context in the runtime notes; if contribution and branch protections materially constrain attacker-controlled code paths, some findings may narrow but not disappear."
  ]
}
